What:		/sys/bus/spi/devices/.../flush_stats
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	ESP32-S31 Linux maintainers
Description:
		Read-only CO5300 framebuffer flush statistics. Output consists of
		newline-separated key=value fields in four lines.

		flushes counts attempted dirty-range and panel_reinit_draw flushes;
		errors counts failed flushes. rows gives the last logical first..last
		row range and bytes is the requested pixel payload, including
		unchanged alignment rows.

		render_us is tiled software rotation time; spi_us includes CASET,
		RASET and the synchronous single-header/quad-pixel message, including
		controller/software wait time; total_us spans both. Times include
		scheduling within the operation, but exclude the deferred-I/O delay.

		full_flushes counts successful full-frame updates. full_render_us,
		full_spi_us and full_total_us retain the latest successful full-frame
		sample even after a partial/cursor update. max_full_us is the maximum
		successful full-frame total since probe. Counters are per device and
		reset at probe. Reading this file neither logs nor flushes.

What:		/sys/bus/spi/devices/.../spi_freq_hz
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	ESP32-S31 Linux maintainers
Description:
		Read/write requested SPI frequency in decimal Hz. Accessible also
		through /sys/class/graphics/fbN/device/spi_freq_hz. Accepts nonzero
		values in the SPI controller's min_speed_hz..max_speed_hz range;
		invalid values return EINVAL. Defaults to spi-max-frequency in DT
		(40000000 on this board). Hardware divider rounding may lower the
		actual clock. A write waits for an active window to finish and
		changes subsequent transfers; no reboot is needed. Frequencies
		above 40 MHz have not been board-tested. Resets at probe/reboot.

What:		/sys/bus/spi/devices/.../rotation
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	ESP32-S31 Linux maintainers
Description:
		Read/write software rotation in degrees relative to landscape.
		Accessible also through /sys/class/graphics/fbN/device/rotation.
		At the default DT rotation 0, accepts 0 or 180 without changing
		the 502x410 framebuffer, stride or fbcon layout. Writes schedule a
		complete refresh. Portrait requires DT rotation = <90> or <270>
		and a kernel/DTB rebuild and reboot; the framebuffer then becomes
		410x502 and runtime writes accept 90 or 270. Other values and
		changes between portrait/landscape return EINVAL. The GRAM window
		alignment and the symmetric 40-pixel content inset are preserved.
		Resets to the DT setting at probe/reboot. Reading does not flush.

What:		/sys/bus/spi/devices/.../render_stats
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	ESP32-S31 Linux maintainers
Description:
		Read-only pre-SPI rendering measurements. Also accessible through
		/sys/class/graphics/fbN/device/render_stats. Enable measurements
		with /sys/module/co5300fb/parameters/render_diagnostics (default N).
		Hashing adds CPU work; turn it off after diagnosis. samples counts
		measured frames. rows and bytes describe the last measured payload;
		nonzero_bytes counts nonzero payload bytes and hash is FNV-1a-32.
		The fixed sample (265,240) reports fb_rgb565, tx_rgb565 and its
		tx_offset in that payload when sample_valid=Y. A full 502x410 frame
		at rotation 0 puts this pixel at byte 217638. The sample is the
		white belly of the positioned login Tux (ffff). rotation describes
		the measured frame. reset_raw is the current physical RST GPIO level
		(1 releases reset); negative values are GPIO read errors. Samples
		inspect CPU memory before submission and do not prove on-wire data
		or panel reception. Reading neither draws nor sends SPI commands.

What:		/sys/bus/spi/devices/.../panel_resume
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	ESP32-S31 Linux maintainers
Description:
		Write-only, explicit panel-state diagnostic/recovery. Also accessible
		through /sys/class/graphics/fbN/device/panel_resume. Writing decimal
		1 waits for the active window, sends SLPOUT (11h), waits 120 ms,
		then restores brightness control (53h=20h), normal/HBM brightness
		(51h=ffh, 63h=ffh) and DISPON (29h). It schedules a full redraw only
		after every command succeeds. It does not reset GPIO, replace the
		supplier init sequence or clear framebuffer memory. A physically low
		RST returns EHOSTDOWN; GPIO/SPI errors propagate. Other writes return
		EINVAL. It runs only on explicit request; a black frame does not
		trigger automatic recovery. Success is SPI submission, not proof
		that the panel accepted the command. Root permission is required.

What:		/sys/bus/spi/devices/.../panel_test
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	ESP32-S31 Linux maintainers
Description:
		Write-only direct panel test, also accessible through
		/sys/class/graphics/fbN/device/panel_test. Decimal 1 fills the full
		GRAM window with red RGB565 f800; 2 writes full black followed by a
		centered green RGB565 07e0 rectangle. On the standard landscape
		board, full CASET/RASET are 22..431/0..501 (411640 payload bytes).
		The green rectangle uses 124..327/126..375 (102000 payload bytes).
		All starts and extents are even. Native window dimensions follow
		the configured geometry/rotation. No framebuffer memory is read or
		modified and the renderer is bypassed; the same command/RAMWR and
		SPI/GDMA paths are used as normal flushes.

		The pattern is held: normal fbcon/deferred flushes send no SPI while
		active, so cursor work cannot erase it. Console input and framebuffer
		memory updates continue. Write 0 to release and request a full redraw
		of the current framebuffer. SPI failures release the hold, request a
		redraw and propagate the error. Invalid requests return EINVAL. The
		test is inactive by default and is never triggered automatically.

What:		/sys/bus/spi/devices/.../panel_test_stats
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	ESP32-S31 Linux maintainers
Description:
		Read-only direct-test state/counters. active/mode describe the hold;
		last_mode/runs/errors/last_error describe direct test attempts.
		windows/bytes count successful RAMWR submissions in the last test
		run; columns/rows/color describe its last attempted window. Standard
		mode 1 succeeds with windows=1 bytes=411640; mode 2 succeeds with
		windows=2 bytes=513640. Reinitialization replay counts as another run.
		These counts do not prove physical panel reception. Normal flush_stats
		and render_stats do not count direct tests. Reading sends no commands.

What:		/sys/bus/spi/devices/.../panel_te_off
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	ESP32-S31 Linux maintainers
Description:
		Write-only explicit TE-off experiment. Decimal 1 sends DCS 34h with
		no parameter and schedules a redraw. DCS 35h with parameter 00h is
		TE-on with vertical-blank output, not TE-off. The standard probe
		sequence already uses parameterless 34h. This control resends TE-off
		without releasing an active panel_test.
		SPI errors propagate; other values return EINVAL. No automatic use.

What:		/sys/bus/spi/devices/.../panel_reinit
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	ESP32-S31 Linux maintainers
Description:
		Write-only manual full reinitialization. Decimal 1 waits for the
		current window, pulses physical reset low for 10..11 ms, releases
		reset, waits 150 ms, replays the same validated supplier init used at
		probe (including its delays), then sends DISPON. With the standard
		sequence this restores FE/C4/3A/34/53/51/63/11/29 and takes about
		760 ms plus transport. TE-off (34h) has no parameter, including at
		probe; the other supplier commands and delays retain their order.
		An active direct pattern is replayed after success; otherwise a full
		framebuffer redraw is queued. Failure releases the test hold and
		queues a framebuffer redraw. GPIO/SPI/sequence errors propagate;
		other values return EINVAL. Recovery logs are kept out of fbcon so
		they do not overwrite login memory. Runs only on explicit request.

What:		/sys/bus/spi/devices/.../panel_reinit_draw
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	ESP32-S31 Linux maintainers
Description:
		Write-only synchronous framebuffer recovery, also accessible through
		/sys/class/graphics/fbN/device/panel_reinit_draw. Writing decimal 1
		waits for the active window, releases any panel_test hold, pulses
		physical reset and replays the full supplier init exactly as
		panel_reinit does. It then renders the current framebuffer and sends
		one full CASET/RASET/RAMWR before returning, retaining io_lock across
		reset, initialization, rendering and the synchronous SPI transfer.
		It neither queues deferred work nor modifies framebuffer memory.
		Existing pending framebuffer work remains pending.

		The standard sequence disables TE with parameterless 34h. A standard
		landscape frame uses columns 22..431, rows 0..501 and 411640 payload
		bytes. Normal flush_stats count this full-frame attempt; render_stats
		also measure it when render_diagnostics is enabled. Reset/init errors
		occur before the flush and are returned without a flush_stats sample.
		Times in flush_stats exclude reset and supplier initialization delays.

		Missing framebuffer/transfer buffers return ENODEV before reset and
		preserve the test hold; other requests return EINVAL. GPIO, supplier
		sequence and SPI errors propagate. After reset/transfer failure the
		test hold stays released; no deferred replacement is queued. Runtime
		command logs are suppressed so fbcon cannot overwrite login pixels.
		Success reports completed SPI submission, not panel reception. Root
		permission is required. Runs only on explicit request.
